{"author":{"id":"746a4d30afc20b78119cb8ed7c194f988174fc252f0e9d9eb92022244ef86db3"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1775230583,"nonce":"MZRp9hpd8Lq+qdZmezfAH+KLnFc=","metadata":{"github-id":"I_kwDOK4fCvM76Z3Nq","github-url":"https://github.com/rolker/unh_echoboats_project11/issues/39","origin":"github"},"title":"Check IzzyBoat router for same DNS forwarding issue as BizzyBoat","message":"## Summary\n\nCheck IzzyBoat's router for the same DNS forwarding issue found on BizzyBoat's router.\n\n## Background\n\nOn BizzyBoat, dnsmasq had hardcoded `server=8.8.8.8/8.8.4.4/1.1.1.1` entries. When\nStarlink (WAN) was down and the router failed over to cell via mwan3, DNS queries from\ndnsmasq itself still went out the dead WAN interface because locally-originated traffic\nbypasses mwan3 firewall marks. Result: external DNS resolution failed for all LAN clients.\n\n**Fix applied on BizzyBoat**: removed hardcoded `server=` entries so dnsmasq relies\nsolely on the auto-populated resolv file from active interfaces.\n\n## Action\n\n- SSH to IzzyBoat router\n- Check for hardcoded DNS servers: `uci show dhcp.@dnsmasq[0].server`\n- If present, remove them:\n  ```\n  uci delete dhcp.\u003csection\u003e.server\n  uci commit dhcp\n  /etc/init.d/dnsmasq restart\n  ```\n- Verify external DNS works when only cell/VPN is available\n\n---\n**Authored-By**: `Claude Code Agent`\n**Model**: `Claude Opus 4.6`","files":null}]}